  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInAndImportantAdditionsToFranchiseRightsTextBlock id="Tag9" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInAndImportantAdditionsToFranchiseRightsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfAcquisitionOfOwnershipInOtherCompaniesByReorganizationMergerOrConsolidationWithOtherCompaniesTextBlock id="Tag10" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfAcquisitionOfOwnershipInOtherCompaniesByReorganizationMergerOrConsolidationWithOtherCompaniesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfPurchaseOrSaleOfAnOperatingUnitOrSystemTextBlock id="Tag11" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfPurchaseOrSaleOfAnOperatingUnitOrSystemTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantLeaseholdsThatHaveBeenAcquiredOrGivenAssignedOrSurrenderedTextBlock id="Tag12" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantLeaseholdsThatHaveBeenAcquiredOrGivenAssignedOrSurrenderedTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantExtensionOrReductionOfTransmissionOrDistributionSystemTextBlock id="Tag13" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="Normal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;Effective April 1, 2026, City of Farmington, Colorado Springs Utilities, Deseret Generation &amp;amp; Transmission Co-operative, Platte River Power Authority, Western Area Power Administration - Colorado River Storage Project, and Western Area Power Administration - Rocky Mountain Region all became transmission owning members.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="Normal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;Effective April 1, 2026, Enterprise Products Operating, LLC and Grid United LLC became non-transmission owning members.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="Normal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;"&gt;Effective May 1, 2026, Highline Transmission, LLC became a non-transmission owning member.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="Normal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;"&gt;Effective June 1, 2026, Fresh Energy, ONEOK Gas Transportation, L.L.C., ONEOK Rockies Midstream, L.L.C., and &lt;/font&gt;Orsted&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;"&gt; Onshore North America, LLC became non-transmission owning members.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantExtensionOrReductionOfTransmissionOrDistributionSystemTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock id="Tag14" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;Southwest Power Pool (SPP) has a $150,000,000 revolving line of credit with a commercial bank expiring in 2033 &lt;em&gt;(Docket number ES25-33)&lt;/em&gt;. At June 30, 2026, $34,800,000 was borrowed against this line. The agreement has a variable interest rate based on the Daily Simple Secured Overnight Funding Rate (SOFR) index plus a credit margin that varies according to cash collateral provided to secure the loan. The margin applicable at June 30, 2026, was 2.80% resulting in an effective rate of 6.41%. The Company&amp;#8217;s line of credit requires compliance with certain financial and non-financial covenants as well as periodic reporting requirements. &lt;font style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif; color: black;"&gt;SPP &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;has a $30,000,000 revolving line of credit with a commercial bank expiring in 2027 &lt;em&gt;(Docket number ES25-51)&lt;/em&gt;. At June 30, 2026, $52,908 was borrowed against this line. The agreement has a variable interest rate based on the Daily Simple Secured Overnight Funding Rate (SOFR) index plus a 1.1% credit margin. The Company&amp;#8217;s line of credit requires compliance with certain financial and non-financial covenants as well as periodic reporting requirements.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif; color: black;"&gt;SPP &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;has an $80,000,000 revolving commitment from another commercial bank expiring in 2027 that could be utilized for both revolving and term loans &lt;em&gt;(Docket number ES22-33)&lt;/em&gt;. At June 30, 2026, $40,800,000 was outstanding against the revolving balance and $30,457,632 was outstanding against the term loan principal. The agreement has a revolving interest rate based on the Secured Overnight Funding Rate (SOFR) index plus a 1.5% credit margin, with a floor of 2.50%. The Company&amp;#8217;s line of credit requires compliance with certain financial and non-financial covenants as well as periodic reporting requirements.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock id="Tag15" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock>
